 :design
 {:ceiling "One task-owned fixed NBB harness and one fixed data manifest outside both owner repositories; no copied validator, copied producer, owner edit, additional dependency assumption, or effect fixture. No files created by this plan except this plan."
  :binding "Parent independently supplies expected identity with adapter-revision equal to the verified Oikos core SHA-256 above and validator-revision equal to the independently verified Services validator SHA-256 above. Verify all fixed binding fields against core constants, source objects and parent handoff; do not use test a/b fake revisions or derive trust merely from the artifact. Binding is comparison data, not authentication."
  :inputs "Fixed manifest carries the complete literal vector table and separate per-implementation expectations; no arbitrary scripts, network input, private data, or dynamic test generation except explicit bounded repeats. Lock its bytes and harness SHA-256 before review."
  :producer "Call actual render with each positive string and supplied binding; require :ok, then extract its exact :payload-bytes and :descriptor-bytes, counts, hashes and source-binding. Check counts and SHA-256 independently over raw bytes, and send those unmodified bytes, descriptor first, to real pinned Python validate. Also call actual Oikos validate on the complete produced record; no roundtrip-only compatibility claim."
  :negative "Manifest supplies explicit raw payload/descriptor byte pairs, including malformed UTF-8. Independently compute byte counts and SHA-256 over each raw pair and assemble a complete artifact with the external binding; call Oikos validate and separately call real Python validate on exactly those bytes. Compare each with its own declared expectation, not a blanket equal-verdict rule."
  :ipc "Harness sends bounded base64 pairs to a fixed Python -c program on stdin; Python imports the exact pinned local_generation_edn and wire from a verified read-only source directory, decodes with strict base64, calls validate(descriptor, payload), returns only indexed booleans. Never pass payload in argv or print payload. Internal IPC has a separately bounded allowance sufficient for all vectors; final stdout/stderr together <=4096 bytes, otherwise fail."
  :commands ["<pinned-nbb> -cp <verified-oikos-src> <fixed-harness.cljs> <fixed-manifest>" "<pinned-python3> -I -B -c <fixed-reviewed-literal> <verified-services-scripts-dir>"]
  :python-import "The fixed -c literal explicitly inserts only the verified scripts directory into sys.path, imports local_generation_edn (which imports sibling wire), processes framed stdin and emits booleans; -I ignores ambient Python paths and -B disables bytecode writes. No shell, Bash, shx, facade, runner or filesystem engine."
  :limits "External supervisor enforces monotonic 10s wall-clock and 256 MiB per process including descendants; kill on timeout, excess memory/output, malformed framing, nonzero exit or missing result. Separately bound fixed vector count, each raw input <=65536 bytes and IPC size; no payloads in evidence. Resource feasibility must be demonstrated, not silently relaxed."
  :closure "Before execution independently pin and verify Git commit/tree and actual bytes of the complete transitive Oikos source/classpath and NBB/Node runtime/dependency closure, exact Python executable, standard-library and native-library closure, Services validator/wire bytes, harness and manifest. Capture version, resolved paths and hashes; reject unexpected imports, mutable drift and unavailable offline closure. Run with cleared environment, verified read-only inputs, no credentials, network, installation or source build; supervisor enforces isolation. No dependency is assumed needed beyond verified existing closures."
  :red "A substituted validator that always returns true or false must fail negative or positive assertions; substituted render that returns a fixed golden must fail distinct positive vectors. Pin mismatch, swapped arguments, truncated IPC, changed bytes or hashes, malformed result, and nonzero/timeout are failures, not skips. Fault-injection controls are harness self-checks, not substitutes for the genuine pinned validator run."}
 :fixed-vectors
 {:positive ["empty string" "lambda ASCII" "quote and backslash" "tab newline carriage return and U+0001" "λ" "😀" "32767 and 32768 ASCII bytes" "10915 U+0001 plus a, descriptor 65536 bytes"]
  :positive-expectation "render :ok, Oikos validate :ok, Python True for every actual produced pair; record indexed counts and digests only. The 65536 boundary follows 45 + 6*10915 + 1."
  :negative-both-reject ["payload #inst or #= reader form" "payload extra or duplicate map key" "payload number instead of string" "payload escaped slash" "payload trailing junk" "descriptor duplicate value key" "descriptor extra key" "descriptor wrong schema or numeric value" "descriptor value differs from payload" "NUL value" "invalid UTF-8 bytes C0 80 in either side"]
  :negative-oikos-only ["payload canonical golden without newline: Python True, Oikos error" "payload double space before string: Python True, Oikos error" "descriptor leading whitespace: Python True, Oikos error" "descriptor lambda with initial l encoded as \\u006c: Python True, Oikos error"]
  :negative-rule "All unmentioned side bytes use literal canonical lambda golden. Manifest must spell exact byte strings, expected booleans and raw SHA-256 values; review every case against source before execution. Never claim Python rejects all noncanonical Oikos artifacts."}
 :admission
 ["1. Parent independently verifies immutable object and runtime closure, exact manifest expectations, external revision binding and feasible resource supervisor; review harness and manifest without execution."
  "2. Separate authorization for bounded offline synthetic invocation; run RED controls and then genuine comparison; retain indexed results, command identities, source pins, exit/resource observations and pre/post hashes without payloads."
  "3. Independent review of evidence can at most admit compatibility for the explicitly enumerated positive byte pairs and record per-vector negative observations; no general equivalence or authorization follows."
  "4. Policy-bound end-to-end filesystem/effect fixture remains HELD pending separate design, authorization, binding and review; no Services runtime build, mutation, deployment, model, approval or board action here."]
